# Merge lane for every repository this machine hosts (sd:3003). One job file,
# the same on every machine: `lane run --hosted` runs the lane of each managed
# repository whose lane host is this machine, one after another. `NULL` means
# the hub. Move a repository's lane with `sd-db.sh repo lane-host <path>
# <host>|hub` or the dashboard's Move lane control; the next run follows it.
# It replaces one job file per repository, hub or satellite.
#
# It needs no `-C`: it reads the repo table, not a working folder. A lane
# whose runner lock is held is skipped and never waited for. The job drains
# each queue and exits; it is not a poller, and an empty queue exits 0 at once.
# A slot that finds this job's own run still active logs `skipped` and exits 0.
#
# JOB_TIMEOUT is above one lane run on purpose (review, `make check` and a
# merge take 30-60 minutes): a limit below that could stop a merge part way.
# Lanes run one after another, so a long run delays the next lane to a later slot.
#
# SD_PACK_ROOT is escaped so the `bash -c` that runs the command reads it,
# after ~/.config/shell/env.sh; this file is sourced before env.sh is.
JOB_SCHEDULE="*/5 * * * *"
JOB_TIMEOUT="120m"
JOB_COMMAND="\"\${SD_PACK_ROOT:-\$HOME/repos/platypeeps/sd-ai-command-pack}/bin/sd-ship\" lane run --hosted"
